# The Dockerfile only ever COPYs requirements.txt — everything else (source
# code, data, thesis media, R analysis, .git history) is bind-mounted at
# runtime, not baked into the image.
#
# docker build packages the ENTIRE build context and sends it to the Docker
# daemon before a single Dockerfile instruction runs — COPY just reaches
# into that already-received bundle afterward. Without this file, the whole
# repo (thesis PDFs, .git history, data/) would get packaged and transferred
# upfront, only for 99.9% of it to sit unused for the rest of the build.
# Excluding it here means it's never packaged or sent in the first place,
# not just ignored after arrival.
*
!requirements.txt
